","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-22.1% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 97 companies in the universe; the top four hold 26% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted lower, down 7% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has rebounded 6% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 18% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 32% and a beta of 0.62, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.24 vs 5y 0.52), so read it loosely.","About $33.9M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 27% in the 2020 crash and 25% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 68% below its DCF fair value of $107, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 67%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $25.55 to $287 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Utilities peers: P/E 44.3 vs 20.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 219% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.3% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 0.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 14 covering analysts target $40.36 on average, 18% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 6.4%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.79).","It converts 26% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 4.07x.","ROE of 9% is amplified by 8.7x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 9.6x net debt to EBITDA ($231.0M of cash against $8.3B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 0.4x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.54 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.3% over 3 years, 3.6% over 5 years and 5.1% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 25%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -2.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-2.5% trend).","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (22.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 51, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.7%), and institutions hold 91%.","It returns 4.8% a year to shareholders (5.5% in dividends, less 0.7% of net share issuance).","It pays out 237% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["Compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":44,"head":"Avoid: operating income covers interest only 0.4x.","pros":["Trades 68% below fair value of $107","FCF margin 25.8%","14 analysts' mean target $40.36 (+18%)","Returns 4.8% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["ROIC 2.5% vs WACC 6.4%","Net debt/EBITDA 9.6x","Interest coverage only 0.4x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 44.3x vs sector 20.4x"],"flags":["Operating income covers interest only 0.4x"],"need":[],"buy_below":90.57,"vc":{"base":106.55,"base_src":"dcf","bear":25.55,"bull":287.28,"alt_median":33.49,"n_alt":2,"gap":3.9021,"dispersion":0.6706,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (67% dispersion)","DCF is 390% above the other models' median ($33.49)","bull case is 11.2x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":20.4014,"ev_ebitda":12.539,"pfcf":19.6541,"pb":1.8576,"roic":0.0568,"gross_margin":0.3591,"fcf_margin":-0.0633,"div_yield":0.0329}},"ticker":"CWEN","date":"2026